{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794865326456,"sessionID":"ses_e19b0e5bfffekS89YIWXLEKMH9","part":{"partID":"prt_1e64f64a7001yYb2rcExvIUOgW","sessionID":"ses_e19b0e5bfffekS89YIWXLEKMH9","messageID":"msg_1e64f4b4f001a6g1GiqO2toI0z","type":"tool","id":"call_ef3fd4dee9af4ebf9256a063","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cat specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-brief-13.txt 2>&1 || echo \"BRIEF_MISSING\"","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"Code review pass thirteen of command surfacing. Scope: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-scope-13.txt lists files as area TAB path. Your lineage label is the last folder of config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir: mention-13 reviews area mention, data-13 reviews area data. mention covers commandOnlyMentioned, which now drops brackets, parentheses, tildes, code tags, guillemets and primes, skips a doc-path occurrence, reads a refusal of 'it' after the name, and reads a command named as a document after the, this or that; and typedCommandIn, whose start boundary now takes the same marks. Look for a request that now reads as a mention (a false refusal stops a command the reader asked for), and for a refusal or question shape still read as a request. data covers seven new advisor intent_signals phrases, one playbook prompt change and ADR-001, which keeps the stale-graph probe on /doctor:helper. Check that the phrases cannot pull ordinary prompts to the advisor and that the playbook prompt matches its expected lines.\n\nCover all four dimensions (correctness, security, traceability, maintainability), and review every scope file of your area under at least two of them.\n\nRun each iteration as the deep-review workflow defines it, including its graph and stop steps, which earlier passes skipped:\n1. Write the iteration record to your state log with dimensions, filesReviewed, findingsNew, newFindingsRatio and a graphEvents array: one dimension node per dimension you covered, one file node per file you read, one finding node per finding, one evidence node per finding naming its file:line, and edges COVERS (dimension to file), IN_DIMENSION and IN_FILE (finding to dimension and file) and EVIDENCE_FOR (evidence to finding). The shape is in .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state-jsonl.md under Graph Events.\n2. Persist them: node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/upsert.cjs --spec-folder specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build --loop-type review --session-id <your config sessionId> --nodes '<json array>' --edges '<json array>', with kind and relation upper case.\n3. Decide whether to stop: node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs --spec-folder specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build --loop-type review --session-id <your config sessionId> --convergence-mode default --stop-decision --config-path <absolute path of your deep-review-config.json> --state-log <absolute path of your deep-review-state.jsonl> --registry-path <absolute path of your deep-review-findings-registry.json> --iteration-count <iterations done> --security-sensitive-fix-scope false --fix-replay-required-rows 0 --fix-replay-passing-rows 0. Record its decision, stopReason and blockedBy in an event line of your state log. When the decision is STOP, synthesize and end with that stopReason; otherwise continue, aiming the next iteration at what blockedBy or the graph trace names.\n\nDo not re-report these recorded limits unless you show a new input that breaks them: a suffix followed by a file extension such as :auto.md reads as the command, as it did before this branch; a node -e arrow inside escaped quotes still reads as a redirect; isolation-check.sh is macOS only. Underscore emphasis around a command name is not dropped, because a command name may hold an underscore. The two moved baseline rows are judged without their text: 038-alignment-p1-remediation/scratch/lead-diag.mjs prints only lead indices. The open P2 list in 038-alignment-p1-remediation/scratch/alignment-final-dispositions.md and the open P2 of review passes ten to twelve (review-report-pass-10.md, review-report-pass-11.md, review-report.md) are already recorded. The holdout gate is read by its count only, never its rows. Every finding is P0, P1 or P2 with file:line and a concrete input that shows it. HOLDOUT RULE: never open command-prompts.jsonl, holdout-prompts.jsonl or behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl except through jq 'del(.prompt)', never run git diff, show or log -p over a path that includes them without the pathspecs ':(exclude)**/command-prompts.jsonl' ':(exclude)**/holdout-prompts.jsonl' ':(exclude)**/behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl', never run score-command-transcripts.mjs --summary, and never print session text from a CLI session store. Never read or create .skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env. The reviewer changes no code; it writes only inside its lineage folder and through the two scripts above.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Code review pass thirteen of command surfacing. Scope: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-scope-13.txt lists files as area TAB path. Your lineage label is the last folder of config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir: mention-13 reviews area mention, data-13 reviews area data. mention covers commandOnlyMentioned, which now drops brackets, parentheses, tildes, code tags, guillemets and primes, skips a doc-path occurrence, reads a refusal of 'it' after the name, and reads a command named as a document after the, this or that; and typedCommandIn, whose start boundary now takes the same marks. Look for a request that now reads as a mention (a false refusal stops a command the reader asked for), and for a refusal or question shape still read as a request. data covers seven new advisor intent_signals phrases, one playbook prompt change and ADR-001, which keeps the stale-graph probe on /doctor:helper. Check that the phrases cannot pull ordinary prompts to the advisor and that the playbook prompt matches its expected lines.\n\nCover all four dimensions (correctness, security, traceability, maintainability), and review every scope file of your area under at least two of them.\n\nRun each iteration as the deep-review workflow defines it, including its graph and stop steps, which earlier passes skipped:\n1. Write the iteration record to your state log with dimensions, filesReviewed, findingsNew, newFindingsRatio and a graphEvents array: one dimension node per dimension you covered, one file node per file you read, one finding node per finding, one evidence node per finding naming its file:line, and edges COVERS (dimension to file), IN_DIMENSION and IN_FILE (finding to dimension and file) and EVIDENCE_FOR (evidence to finding). The shape is in .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state-jsonl.md under Graph Events.\n2. Persist them: node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/upsert.cjs --spec-folder specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build --loop-type review --session-id <your config sessionId> --nodes '<json array>' --edges '<json array>', with kind and relation upper case.\n3. Decide whether to stop: node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs --spec-folder specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build --loop-type review --session-id <your config sessionId> --convergence-mode default --stop-decision --config-path <absolute path of your deep-review-config.json> --state-log <absolute path of your deep-review-state.jsonl> --registry-path <absolute path of your deep-review-findings-registry.json> --iteration-count <iterations done> --security-sensitive-fix-scope false --fix-replay-required-rows 0 --fix-replay-passing-rows 0. Record its decision, stopReason and blockedBy in an event line of your state log. When the decision is STOP, synthesize and end with that stopReason; otherwise continue, aiming the next iteration at what blockedBy or the graph trace names.\n\nDo not re-report these recorded limits unless you show a new input that breaks them: a suffix followed by a file extension such as :auto.md reads as the command, as it did before this branch; a node -e arrow inside escaped quotes still reads as a redirect; isolation-check.sh is macOS only. Underscore emphasis around a command name is not dropped, because a command name may hold an underscore. The two moved baseline rows are judged without their text: 038-alignment-p1-remediation/scratch/lead-diag.mjs prints only lead indices. The open P2 list in 038-alignment-p1-remediation/scratch/alignment-final-dispositions.md and the open P2 of review passes ten to twelve (review-report-pass-10.md, review-report-pass-11.md, review-report.md) are already recorded. The holdout gate is read by its count only, never its rows. Every finding is P0, P1 or P2 with file:line and a concrete input that shows it. HOLDOUT RULE: never open command-prompts.jsonl, holdout-prompts.jsonl or behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl except through jq 'del(.prompt)', never run git diff, show or log -p over a path that includes them without the pathspecs ':(exclude)**/command-prompts.jsonl' ':(exclude)**/holdout-prompts.jsonl' ':(exclude)**/behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl', never run score-command-transcripts.mjs --summary, and never print session text from a CLI session store. Never read or create .skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env. The reviewer changes no code; it writes only inside its lineage folder and through the two scripts above.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cat specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-brief-13.txt 2>&1 || echo \\\"BRIEF_MISSING\\\"\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794865325223,"end":1794865326456}}}}
