{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794865941052,"sessionID":"ses_e19b0e5bfffekS89YIWXLEKMH9","part":{"partID":"prt_1e6584a9e001JB9VGByZMJu03P","sessionID":"ses_e19b0e5bfffekS89YIWXLEKMH9","messageID":"msg_1e658210b001jBGBz1RAvtK7zH","type":"tool","id":"call_aa2a9ca8bc6f4d6eab2947dc","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 001\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Mode: review, lineage `data-13`, iteration 1 of 8.\n- Declared target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder).\n- Area: `data` per `review/review-scope-13.txt`; diff range `b8ebee37d75..932aff4e437`.\n- Focus this iteration: correctness and traceability of the seven new advisor `intent_signals` phrases, the CL-009 playbook prompt change and ADR-001's P05 waiver.\n- Operator review focus binding: `review_brief-13.txt` was read first; every finding below is checked against its data-area questions (ordinary prompts must not be pulled to the advisor, the playbook prompt must match its expected lines, ADR-001 must keep P05 on `/doctor:helper`).\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/graph-metadata.json:1-201` (whole file at `932aff4e437`)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/graph-metadata.json:96-110` (the seven appended signals)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/cli-hooks-and-plugin/brief-command-policy-word.md:1-198` (whole file at `932aff4e437`)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/cli-hooks-and-plugin/brief-command-policy-word.md:80-165` (changed prompt and Expected block)\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/040-final-alignment-loop/decision-record.md:1-38`\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/040-final-alignment-loop/acceptance-criteria.md:59`\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/040-final-alignment-loop/tasks.md:37,49,121`\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/040-final-alignment-loop/scratch/probes.json:79-135`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/skill-graph.json` (the compiled `system-skill-advisor` signals)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/command-bridges.generated.json:2116-2140` and its `commandPolicies` rows for `/doctor:update`\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml:786-809`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/lanes/explicit.ts:1-330`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/projection.ts:295-300`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:200-290`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:64-200` (`command-doctor-update` row)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/scorer/declared-phrase-specificity.vitest.ts:30-90`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/dist/runtime/lib/scorer/{fusion,projection}.js` (the built scorer used for the scoring probes)\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-brief-13.txt:1-1`\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-scope-13.txt:1-7`\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/data-13/deep-review-config.json`\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\n1. **New signals are indexed as common words, so ordinary prompts top the advisor** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/graph-metadata.json:101-107` -- Five of the seven appended signals introduce ordinary vocabulary (`clean`, `arena`, `arm`, `advisor`, `briefs`) that the lexical lane consumes as skill tokens. Prompts that never name the advisor now return it as the top recommendation at confidence 0.82 with `passes_threshold: true`, and in two cases it displaces the plausible skill.\n   Finding class: algorithmic\n   Scope proof: Scored the same prompt set twice with the built scorer, once with the committed projection and once with the seven signals removed from the advisor's `intentSignals`. `the routing arm of the load balancer is flaky` -> `system-skill-advisor:0.82` now, `none` before. `the advisor briefs me every morning` -> `system-skill-advisor:0.82` now, `none` before. `the arena is clean now` -> `system-skill-advisor:0.82` now, `none` before. `clean the routing table` -> `system-skill-advisor:0.82` now, `none` before. `fix the routing arm in the nginx config` puts the advisor first at 0.82 where `system-spec-kit`/`sk-code` led before.\n   Affected surface hints: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/graph-metadata.json`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/skill-graph.json`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/lanes/lexical.ts`\n   Case: `the routing arm of the load balancer is flaky`\n   Claim adjudication: `{\"type\":\"algorithmic\",\"claim\":\"The appended intent_signals leak common tokens into the lexical lane, so prompts with no advisor intent pass the 0.82 threshold for system-skill-advisor.\",\"evidenceRefs\":[\"graph-metadata.json:101-107\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/skill-graph.json (signals for system-skill-advisor)\",\"dist scorer probe: laneContributions lexical rawScore 0.67 evidence token:clean, token:arena\"],\"counterevidenceSought\":\"Tested controls with the same words in other senses; checked whether the 0.82 confidence is below the emitted threshold and found passes_threshold true with uncertainty 0.12-0.16. Checked whether the same prompts topped the advisor before the change: they returned none in the stripped projection.\",\"alternativeExplanation\":\"The advisor may be the intended catch-all for graph and prompt terminology, so an ordinary networking prompt could be tolerated noise. Rejected because three of the four cases have no advisor/graph meaning at all and two displace a more plausible skill.\",\"finalSeverity\":\"P1\",\"confidence\":0.9,\"downgradeTrigger\":\"If the advisor brief suppresses recommendations below a higher confidence than 0.82, or if the lexical lane already excluded single-token evidence from graph signals before this change.\"}`\n   Recommendation: score joined intent_signals as phrases only, or gate their individual tokens out of the lexical and graph lanes; add ordinary-sense fixtures such as `the routing arm of the load balancer is flaky` and `the advisor briefs me every morning` to the specificity test.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\n1. **`clean arena` fires inside a longer noun phrase and ranks the advisor above a design request** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/graph-metadata.json:106` -- The declared two-word phrase matches as a substring of `clean arena seating`, so a design request is now topped by the advisor at 0.82 ahead of `sk-design`, where `sk-design` was the only recommendation before.\n   Finding class: algorithmic\n   Scope proof: `clean arena seating chart for the stadium` -> `system-skill-advisor:0.82` first, `sk-design:0.82` second; the stripped-intent projection returned only `sk-design:0.82`. The recommendation's lanes are `explicit_author:0.88 [author:clean arena]` and `lexical:0.40 [token:clean|token:arena]`.\n   Affected surface hints: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/graph-metadata.json`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/lanes/explicit.ts`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/scorer/declared-phrase-specificity.vitest.ts`\n   Case: `clean arena seating chart for the stadium`\n   Recommendation: require a phrase boundary after a declared signal, or add the ordinary noun-phrase sense as a negative fixture.\n\nNo P0 candidates existed; the P1 above was challenged in-iteration by the stripped-projection control and by the threshold check, and the P2 needed no self-check.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n- `spec_code` -- pass. The committed `intent_signals` block at `932aff4e437` holds 39 phrases and the seven appended ones match T006's description (`tasks.md:49`). The compiled `runtime/scripts/skill-graph.json` carries the same seven strings in the `system-skill-advisor` signals, so the graph recompile claimed by T006 happened.\n- `checklist_evidence` -- pass. `acceptance-criteria.md:59` (AC-004) records P07/P08/P09 passing and P05 topped by `/doctor:helper`; `scratch/probes.json` shows exactly that (`P07` 0.8511, `P08` 0.82, `P09` 0.8548, `P05` `command-doctor-helper` 0.8), and my rerun of P05 returned `command-doctor-helper` at 0.8 with and without the seven signals.\n- `playbook_capability` -- pass. `brief-command-policy-word.md:83-108` sends `check for skilled updates`; scoring that prompt tops `command-doctor-update` (0.8962), and `renderAdvisorBrief` renders `system-skilled-doctor → /doctor:update (ask)` for a parent and `(parent-named only)` for a child, matching `brief-command-policy-word.md:148` and `:160-161`. The old prompt `update skilled to the latest version` tops `sk-git`, which explains why the playbook needed the change.\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- Scorer surface: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:1263` `scoreAdvisorPrompt`; explicit lane `lanes/explicit.ts:309`; lexical lane evidence from `laneContributions`.\n- Command surface: `command-bridges.generated.json` entry `command-doctor-update` and `COMMAND_ROWS['command-doctor-update']` (`command-attach.ts`), policy `ask`, mutating `mutates`, owner `system-skilled-doctor`.\n- Doctor route declaration: `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml:800-809` still lists `update skilled to the latest version`; that phrase no longer reaches its own command (see Edge Cases).\n- ADR surface: `decision-record.md:37` ADR-001 and `acceptance-criteria.md:59` AC-004 agree.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- The phrase `update skilled to the latest version` remains a declared `/doctor:update` trigger (`_routes.yaml:804`) but scores `sk-git` (0.82) and never returns `command-doctor-update`. The playbook now avoids the phrase rather than pinning it. That route file sits outside the declared target, so it is recorded here as integration evidence and left for a follow-up, not raised as a finding against the playbook.\n- `clean arena seating before the show` matched `author:clean arena` yet produced no recommendation (below the 0.82 pass line); the same phrase inside `clean arena seating chart for the stadium` did pass. The difference is the second lexical token (`chart`), so the boundary finding is about ranking, not about every substring occurrence.\n- The committed `derived` block was not regenerated with the seven signals; a fresh `extractDerivedMetadata` run does not surface them either, so this is not evidence of a stale routing surface.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- ADR-001 holds: P05 tops `command-doctor-helper` at 0.8, identical before and after the seven signals, and `/doctor:helper` ranks `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild` first for it.\n- The CL-009 prompt change matches every expected line; the version bumped `1.0.1.0 -> 1.0.2.0`, the six command blocks and the Evidence block all use `check for skilled updates`, and the root catalog row carries no prompt text that would need the same edit.\n- The graph is compiled: `skill-graph.json` signals for `system-skill-advisor` end with the seven new phrases, and the projection reports `source: sqlite` with 61 skills.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- A stale `derived` block breaking routing: the fresh extractor does not add the seven phrases to `trigger_phrases`/`keywords`, so the derived lane is unaffected and the omission is not a routing defect.\n- A secret, injection or ReDoS surface in the change: the signals are static author strings matched by substring/token rules, with no prompt-built regex and no filesystem or credential read.\n- The waived P05 coming back to the advisor through `skill graph is stale` / `rebuild the skill graph`: measured identical 0.8 `command-doctor-helper` ranking before and after; the helper handoff still wins.\n- The playbook prompt itself: its parent and child labels reproduce exactly.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: security and maintainability.\n- Focus area: the same three scope files read under the two remaining dimensions; the phrase specificity contract in `declared-phrase-specificity.vitest.ts`, duplicate/overlapping signals against the doctor vocabulary, and the playbook's own instruction surface.\n- Reason: correctness and traceability are covered; two dimensions remain and each scope file still needs its second dimension.\n- Rotation status: correctness and traceability marked complete for this iteration; security and maintainability next.\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: the lexical-token leak is productive to re-read under maintainability, because its fix shape (phrase-only scoring) changes the declared-phrase contract.\n- Required evidence: a maintainability read of the signal list against the test contract, and a security read of the playbook commands.\n\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/data-13/iterations/iteration-001.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/data-13/iterations/iteration-001.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/data-13/iterations/iteration-001.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Iteration 001\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Mode: review, lineage `data-13`, iteration 1 of 8.\\n- Declared target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder).\\n- Area: `data` per `review/review-scope-13.txt`; diff range `b8ebee37d75..932aff4e437`.\\n- Focus this iteration: correctness and traceability of the seven new advisor `intent_signals` phrases, the CL-009 playbook prompt change and ADR-001's P05 waiver.\\n- Operator review focus binding: `review_brief-13.txt` was read first; every finding below is checked against its data-area questions (ordinary prompts must not be pulled to the advisor, the playbook prompt must match its expected lines, ADR-001 must keep P05 on `/doctor:helper`).\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/graph-metadata.json:1-201` (whole file at `932aff4e437`)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/graph-metadata.json:96-110` (the seven appended signals)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/cli-hooks-and-plugin/brief-command-policy-word.md:1-198` (whole file at `932aff4e437`)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/cli-hooks-and-plugin/brief-command-policy-word.md:80-165` (changed prompt and Expected block)\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/040-final-alignment-loop/decision-record.md:1-38`\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/040-final-alignment-loop/acceptance-criteria.md:59`\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/040-final-alignment-loop/tasks.md:37,49,121`\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/040-final-alignment-loop/scratch/probes.json:79-135`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/skill-graph.json` (the compiled `system-skill-advisor` signals)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/command-bridges.generated.json:2116-2140` and its `commandPolicies` rows for `/doctor:update`\\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml:786-809`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/lanes/explicit.ts:1-330`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/projection.ts:295-300`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:200-290`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:64-200` (`command-doctor-update` row)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/scorer/declared-phrase-specificity.vitest.ts:30-90`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/dist/runtime/lib/scorer/{fusion,projection}.js` (the built scorer used for the scoring probes)\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-brief-13.txt:1-1`\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-scope-13.txt:1-7`\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/data-13/deep-review-config.json`\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\n1. **New signals are indexed as common words, so ordinary prompts top the advisor** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/graph-metadata.json:101-107` -- Five of the seven appended signals introduce ordinary vocabulary (`clean`, `arena`, `arm`, `advisor`, `briefs`) that the lexical lane consumes as skill tokens. Prompts that never name the advisor now return it as the top recommendation at confidence 0.82 with `passes_threshold: true`, and in two cases it displaces the plausible skill.\\n   Finding class: algorithmic\\n   Scope proof: Scored the same prompt set twice with the built scorer, once with the committed projection and once with the seven signals removed from the advisor's `intentSignals`. `the routing arm of the load balancer is flaky` -> `system-skill-advisor:0.82` now, `none` before. `the advisor briefs me every morning` -> `system-skill-advisor:0.82` now, `none` before. `the arena is clean now` -> `system-skill-advisor:0.82` now, `none` before. `clean the routing table` -> `system-skill-advisor:0.82` now, `none` before. `fix the routing arm in the nginx config` puts the advisor first at 0.82 where `system-spec-kit`/`sk-code` led before.\\n   Affected surface hints: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/graph-metadata.json`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/skill-graph.json`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/lanes/lexical.ts`\\n   Case: `the routing arm of the load balancer is flaky`\\n   Claim adjudication: `{\\\"type\\\":\\\"algorithmic\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"The appended intent_signals leak common tokens into the lexical lane, so prompts with no advisor intent pass the 0.82 threshold for system-skill-advisor.\\\",\\\"evidenceRefs\\\":[\\\"graph-metadata.json:101-107\\\",\\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/skill-graph.json (signals for system-skill-advisor)\\\",\\\"dist scorer probe: laneContributions lexical rawScore 0.67 evidence token:clean, token:arena\\\"],\\\"counterevidenceSought\\\":\\\"Tested controls with the same words in other senses; checked whether the 0.82 confidence is below the emitted threshold and found passes_threshold true with uncertainty 0.12-0.16. Checked whether the same prompts topped the advisor before the change: they returned none in the stripped projection.\\\",\\\"alternativeExplanation\\\":\\\"The advisor may be the intended catch-all for graph and prompt terminology, so an ordinary networking prompt could be tolerated noise. Rejected because three of the four cases have no advisor/graph meaning at all and two displace a more plausible skill.\\\",\\\"finalSeverity\\\":\\\"P1\\\",\\\"confidence\\\":0.9,\\\"downgradeTrigger\\\":\\\"If the advisor brief suppresses recommendations below a higher confidence than 0.82, or if the lexical lane already excluded single-token evidence from graph signals before this change.\\\"}`\\n   Recommendation: score joined intent_signals as phrases only, or gate their individual tokens out of the lexical and graph lanes; add ordinary-sense fixtures such as `the routing arm of the load balancer is flaky` and `the advisor briefs me every morning` to the specificity test.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\n1. **`clean arena` fires inside a longer noun phrase and ranks the advisor above a design request** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/graph-metadata.json:106` -- The declared two-word phrase matches as a substring of `clean arena seating`, so a design request is now topped by the advisor at 0.82 ahead of `sk-design`, where `sk-design` was the only recommendation before.\\n   Finding class: algorithmic\\n   Scope proof: `clean arena seating chart for the stadium` -> `system-skill-advisor:0.82` first, `sk-design:0.82` second; the stripped-intent projection returned only `sk-design:0.82`. The recommendation's lanes are `explicit_author:0.88 [author:clean arena]` and `lexical:0.40 [token:clean|token:arena]`.\\n   Affected surface hints: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/graph-metadata.json`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/lanes/explicit.ts`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/scorer/declared-phrase-specificity.vitest.ts`\\n   Case: `clean arena seating chart for the stadium`\\n   Recommendation: require a phrase boundary after a declared signal, or add the ordinary noun-phrase sense as a negative fixture.\\n\\nNo P0 candidates existed; the P1 above was challenged in-iteration by the stripped-projection control and by the threshold check, and the P2 needed no self-check.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n- `spec_code` -- pass. The committed `intent_signals` block at `932aff4e437` holds 39 phrases and the seven appended ones match T006's description (`tasks.md:49`). The compiled `runtime/scripts/skill-graph.json` carries the same seven strings in the `system-skill-advisor` signals, so the graph recompile claimed by T006 happened.\\n- `checklist_evidence` -- pass. `acceptance-criteria.md:59` (AC-004) records P07/P08/P09 passing and P05 topped by `/doctor:helper`; `scratch/probes.json` shows exactly that (`P07` 0.8511, `P08` 0.82, `P09` 0.8548, `P05` `command-doctor-helper` 0.8), and my rerun of P05 returned `command-doctor-helper` at 0.8 with and without the seven signals.\\n- `playbook_capability` -- pass. `brief-command-policy-word.md:83-108` sends `check for skilled updates`; scoring that prompt tops `command-doctor-update` (0.8962), and `renderAdvisorBrief` renders `system-skilled-doctor → /doctor:update (ask)` for a parent and `(parent-named only)` for a child, matching `brief-command-policy-word.md:148` and `:160-161`. The old prompt `update skilled to the latest version` tops `sk-git`, which explains why the playbook needed the change.\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- Scorer surface: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:1263` `scoreAdvisorPrompt`; explicit lane `lanes/explicit.ts:309`; lexical lane evidence from `laneContributions`.\\n- Command surface: `command-bridges.generated.json` entry `command-doctor-update` and `COMMAND_ROWS['command-doctor-update']` (`command-attach.ts`), policy `ask`, mutating `mutates`, owner `system-skilled-doctor`.\\n- Doctor route declaration: `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml:800-809` still lists `update skilled to the latest version`; that phrase no longer reaches its own command (see Edge Cases).\\n- ADR surface: `decision-record.md:37` ADR-001 and `acceptance-criteria.md:59` AC-004 agree.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- The phrase `update skilled to the latest version` remains a declared `/doctor:update` trigger (`_routes.yaml:804`) but scores `sk-git` (0.82) and never returns `command-doctor-update`. The playbook now avoids the phrase rather than pinning it. That route file sits outside the declared target, so it is recorded here as integration evidence and left for a follow-up, not raised as a finding against the playbook.\\n- `clean arena seating before the show` matched `author:clean arena` yet produced no recommendation (below the 0.82 pass line); the same phrase inside `clean arena seating chart for the stadium` did pass. The difference is the second lexical token (`chart`), so the boundary finding is about ranking, not about every substring occurrence.\\n- The committed `derived` block was not regenerated with the seven signals; a fresh `extractDerivedMetadata` run does not surface them either, so this is not evidence of a stale routing surface.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- ADR-001 holds: P05 tops `command-doctor-helper` at 0.8, identical before and after the seven signals, and `/doctor:helper` ranks `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild` first for it.\\n- The CL-009 prompt change matches every expected line; the version bumped `1.0.1.0 -> 1.0.2.0`, the six command blocks and the Evidence block all use `check for skilled updates`, and the root catalog row carries no prompt text that would need the same edit.\\n- The graph is compiled: `skill-graph.json` signals for `system-skill-advisor` end with the seven new phrases, and the projection reports `source: sqlite` with 61 skills.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- A stale `derived` block breaking routing: the fresh extractor does not add the seven phrases to `trigger_phrases`/`keywords`, so the derived lane is unaffected and the omission is not a routing defect.\\n- A secret, injection or ReDoS surface in the change: the signals are static author strings matched by substring/token rules, with no prompt-built regex and no filesystem or credential read.\\n- The waived P05 coming back to the advisor through `skill graph is stale` / `rebuild the skill graph`: measured identical 0.8 `command-doctor-helper` ranking before and after; the helper handoff still wins.\\n- The playbook prompt itself: its parent and child labels reproduce exactly.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: security and maintainability.\\n- Focus area: the same three scope files read under the two remaining dimensions; the phrase specificity contract in `declared-phrase-specificity.vitest.ts`, duplicate/overlapping signals against the doctor vocabulary, and the playbook's own instruction surface.\\n- Reason: correctness and traceability are covered; two dimensions remain and each scope file still needs its second dimension.\\n- Rotation status: correctness and traceability marked complete for this iteration; security and maintainability next.\\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: the lexical-token leak is productive to re-read under maintainability, because its fix shape (phrase-only scoring) changes the declared-phrase contract.\\n- Required evidence: a maintainability read of the signal list against the test contract, and a security read of the playbook commands.\\n\\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/data-13/iterations/iteration-001.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794865908382,"end":1794865941052}}}}
