{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794866542102,"sessionID":"ses_e19b0e5bfffekS89YIWXLEKMH9","part":{"partID":"prt_1e66180f2002xcpOWw9TwqKNoO","sessionID":"ses_e19b0e5bfffekS89YIWXLEKMH9","messageID":"msg_1e6617259001wqEAhB6MZR5rKZ","type":"tool","id":"call_82778a5b61504eb39da94c04","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Report: Command Surfacing Build, Pass Thirteen - data area\n\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder)\n- Pass: the thirteenth review pass, `data` area of `review/review-scope-13.txt`. It read `b8ebee37d75..932aff4e437` for `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/graph-metadata.json`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/cli-hooks-and-plugin/brief-command-policy-word.md` and `040-final-alignment-loop/decision-record.md`, then read each whole file at `932aff4e437`.\n- Lineage: `data-13`, session `fanout-data-13-1794865302020-qunumz`, three iterations, stop reason `converged` at threshold 0.10, `blockedBy` empty. Brief `review/review-brief-13.txt`.\n\n## 1. Executive Summary\n\n- **Overall verdict: CONDITIONAL.** P0 0, P1 1, P2 2 -- the counts the verdict used.\n- **hasAdvisories: false.** Two P2 advisories are open, but the verdict is CONDITIONAL on the active P1, so the advisory flag is not set.\n- **Self-check outcomes.** F001 (P1) was confirmed by the full Hunter/Skeptic/Referee pass in iteration 1: every ordinary-sense prompt returned no skill under the stripped projection and the advisor at 0.82 with `passes_threshold: true` under the committed one. F002 (P2) was confirmed by the same A/B pair on the noun-phrase prompt. F003 (P2) was confirmed by running both shipped scorers on the same prompts. No finding was downgraded or called a false positive.\n- **Review scope summary.** Three files. `graph-metadata.json` gained seven `intent_signals` phrases; the CL-009 playbook changed one prompt in three places and bumped its feature version `1.0.1.0 -> 1.0.2.0`; `decision-record.md` is new and holds ADR-001, which waives AC-004 for probe P05. The graph was recompiled: `skill-graph.json` carries the seven strings.\n- **Operator review focus:** Review pass thirteen. First read specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-brief-13.txt and follow it: it names your area by lineage label, the scope file, the graph and stop steps each iteration runs, and the holdout rule.\n\n## 2. Planning Trigger\n\n`/speckit:plan` is required: the verdict is CONDITIONAL on one active P1.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"triggered\": true,\n  \"verdict\": \"CONDITIONAL\",\n  \"hasAdvisories\": false,\n  \"activeFindings\": [\"F001\", \"F002\", \"F003\"],\n  \"remediationWorkstreams\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"WS-1\",\n      \"findingIds\": [\"F001\"],\n      \"severity\": \"P1\",\n      \"title\": \"Stop indexing common intent-signal words as advisor tokens\",\n      \"scope\": \"graph-metadata intent_signals scoring surface: phrase-only author evidence, or a token stop set for the five generic signals; ordinary-sense fixtures in the specificity test\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"WS-2\",\n      \"findingIds\": [\"F002\"],\n      \"severity\": \"P2\",\n      \"title\": \"Require a phrase boundary after a declared signal\",\n      \"scope\": \"explicit author lane phrase matching for clean arena, plus the noun-phrase fixture\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"WS-3\",\n      \"findingIds\": [\"F003\"],\n      \"severity\": \"P2\",\n      \"title\": \"Pin ordinary-sense prompts across both scorers\",\n      \"scope\": \"declared-phrase-specificity cross-scorer cases and the Python fallback phrase reader\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"specSeed\": [\n    \"State that an intent signal is author evidence for a phrase, and that its individual common words must not become routing tokens on their own.\",\n    \"State that a declared signal matches a request phrase, not a longer noun phrase that happens to contain it.\",\n    \"State that both shipped scorers must agree on the ordinary sense of every declared signal the specificity test pins.\"\n  ],\n  \"planSeed\": [\n    \"Add a phrase-only path or a token stop set for the five generic signals, and add the four ordinary-sense prompts as fixtures.\",\n    \"Require a non-word boundary after a declared signal, or record the ordinary noun-phrase sense as a negative fixture.\",\n    \"Extend the cross-scorer case list with the ordinary-sense prompts and align the Python phrase reader if it disagrees.\"\n  ],\n  \"findingClasses\": [\"algorithmic\", \"algorithmic\", \"test-coverage\"],\n  \"affectedSurfacesSeed\": [\n    \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/graph-metadata.json\",\n    \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/skill-graph.json\",\n    \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/lanes/lexical.ts\",\n    \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/lanes/explicit.ts\",\n    \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/scorer/declared-phrase-specificity.vitest.ts\"\n  ],\n  \"fixCompletenessRequired\": true\n}\n```\n\n## 3. Active Finding Registry\n\n| ID | Severity | Dimension | Location | Finding | Fix recommendation | Finding class | Scope proof | Affected surface hints |\n|----|----------|-----------|----------|---------|--------------------|---------------|-------------|------------------------|\n| F001 | P1 | correctness | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/graph-metadata.json:101` | New signals are indexed as common words, so ordinary prompts top the advisor | Score joined signals as phrases only, or exclude their single tokens from the lexical and graph lanes; add ordinary-sense fixtures | algorithmic | Four ordinary prompts return `system-skill-advisor` 0.82 `passes_threshold: true` with the committed projection and no skill with the seven signals removed | graph metadata, compiled graph, lexical lane, specificity test |\n| F002 | P2 | correctness | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/graph-metadata.json:106` | `clean arena` fires inside a longer noun phrase and ranks the advisor above a design request | Require a phrase boundary after a declared signal, or add the noun-phrase sense as a negative fixture | algorithmic | `clean arena seating chart for the stadium` puts the advisor first at 0.82 and `sk-design` second; stripped projection returned only `sk-design` | graph metadata, explicit lane, specificity test |\n| F003 | P2 | maintainability | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/scorer/declared-phrase-specificity.vitest.ts:169` | The declared-phrase contract holds in one scorer and not the other | Add ordinary-sense prompts as cross-scorer fixtures once the scoring fix lands | test-coverage | The native scorer returns the advisor for `the arena is clean now` and the Python fallback returns no skill; the two pinned phrases do not diverge | specificity test, `skill_advisor.py`, graph metadata |\n\nImpact notes:\n\n- F001 changes the top recommendation, not just a tail entry: `fix the routing arm in the nginx config` puts the advisor ahead of `sk-code`, and `clean arena seating chart for the stadium` puts it ahead of `sk-design`. Every case is advisory only; no command is attached and no mutating command is offered.\n- F002 and F003 are the same signal set seen from two other angles, but each has a separate fix point: phrase boundary, and cross-scorer fixtures.\n\n## 4. Remediation Workstreams\n\n1. **WS-1 (P1)** -- Change how the five generic signals are scored. Keep `routing arm`, `clean arena`, `advisor briefs`, `arena`-family wording as phrase evidence, or drop their single tokens from the lexical and graph lanes. Accept the four ordinary-sense prompts as the regression set.\n2. **WS-2 (P2)** -- Tighten the explicit lane's phrase boundary or record the `clean arena seating ...` sense as a negative fixture.\n3. **WS-3 (P2)** -- Add the ordinary-sense prompts to the cross-scorer case list so the Python fallback and the native scorer cannot drift apart on this class.\n\n## 5. Spec Seed\n\n- A declared intent signal is a phrase contract, not a bag of words.\n- A common collocation is specific only when its context is; the advisor's precision rests on that distinction.\n- Both shipped scorers read the same declared signal list and must agree on its ordinary sense.\n\n## 6. Plan Seed\n\n- Add the phrase-only/token-stop behavior to the signal scoring path and extend `declared-phrase-specificity.vitest.ts` with the four prompts.\n- Add the noun-phrase negative fixture and the boundary rule.\n- Add the cross-scorer fixture and align the Python phrase reader where it disagrees.\n\n## 7. Traceability Status\n\nCore protocols:\n\n- `spec_code`: pass. The seven signals match T006's description (`040/tasks.md:49`) and the compiled `skill-graph.json` carries them; ADR-001 (`decision-record.md:37`), AC-004 (`acceptance-criteria.md:59`) and `probes.json` agree on P05 and P07-P09.\n- `checklist_evidence`: pass. `probes.json` P05 is `command-doctor-helper` at 0.8 and P07/P08/P09 top the advisor; the final-tree rerun reproduces P05 at 0.8.\n\nOverlay protocols:\n\n- `skill_agent`: pass. The authored metadata and the compiled graph carry identical strings; no agent file is in this area.\n- `agent_cross_runtime`: notApplicable. No runtime mirror or agent definition is touched.\n- `feature_catalog_code`: pass. `scorer-fusion/five-lane-fusion.md:27` documents the lexical lane as token overlap, so the observed token behavior matches the documented design; the defect is the signal list's word choice, not the lane.\n- `playbook_capability`: pass. `check for skilled updates` tops `command-doctor-update` at 0.8962 and renders `system-skilled-doctor → /doctor:update (ask)` in a parent and `(parent-named only)` in a child, matching `brief-command-policy-word.md:148` and `:160-161`.\n\n`AC_COVERAGE`: **exempt**. The target spec folder has no `acceptance-criteria.md` and no `implementation-summary.md` at its own level; the phase children own their AC coverage.\n\n## 8. Deferred Items\n\n- The phrase `update skilled to the latest version` is still a declared `/doctor:update` trigger (`_routes.yaml:804`) but scores `sk-git` and never returns its command. The playbook avoids it now. The route file is outside this area, so this is deferred to a routing-area pass, not reported against the playbook.\n- The Python fallback has no command-bridge layer, so P05 there returns `system-skill-advisor` rather than `command-doctor-helper`. That is a scorer-scope difference, not an ADR-001 contradiction.\n- The `derived` block was not regenerated with the seven signals; a fresh extractor run does not add them to `trigger_phrases` or `keywords`, so this is not a stale routing surface.\n- Holdout hygiene is clean for this area: the bridge generator reads route YAML and scorer sources, and `measure-brief-cost.mjs:124` refuses holdout rows.\n\n## Dimension Expansion Map\n\n- Completed pivots: 0. Failed pivots: 0. Audited overrides: 0.\n- Saturated directions: none. Pivot lineage: none.\n- Selected review directions: correctness and traceability (iteration 1), security and maintainability (iteration 2), all four as final verification (iteration 3).\n- Remaining frontier: none. This section records breadth only and does not change the verdict.\n\n## 9. Search Ledger\n\n`*No search-depth state captured (legacy v1 record)*`\n\nThe probes that stand in for a search ledger in this pass:\n\n- Native scorer A/B: committed projection vs the seven signals removed, over eight ordinary prompts; four flip to the advisor, two change rank, two are unchanged.\n- Signal list: 39 entries, 0 duplicates, no control, shell or JSON metacharacter.\n- Playbook: `check for skilled updates` -> `command-doctor-update` 0.8962; old prompt -> `sk-git`; rendered labels match parent and child expectations.\n- ADR: P05 tops `command-doctor-helper` at 0.8 before and after the signals.\n- Cross-scorer: native vs Python over the same prompts; two divergences, both on the new phrases.\n- Holdout: generator input list and the refusal path read; no corpus row reaches a generation or report path.\n- State: three iteration records, three deltas whose first line equals its record, one registry with three open findings, four dimensions covered.\n\n## 10. Audit Appendix\n\n- **Convergence.** Iteration 3 returned `STOP`, `converged`, score 1.0, `blockedBy` `[]`. Ratios were 1.0, 0.1429, 0.0.\n- **Coverage.** 4 of 4 dimensions; core protocols `spec_code` and `checklist_evidence` each recorded; overlay protocols recorded as pass or notApplicable.\n- **Ruled-out claims.** A stale derived block; a holdout leak through bridge generation; secret or environment exposure in the playbook; JSON or shell injection through a signal; duplicate-signal amplification; the waived P05 returning to the advisor; a mid-pass change between iteration 1 and the final tree.\n- **Sources reviewed.** `graph-metadata.json` (whole file and the signal block), `brief-command-policy-word.md` (whole file and the changed ranges), `decision-record.md`, `040/acceptance-criteria.md:59`, `040/tasks.md:37-121`, `040/scratch/probes.json`, `skill-graph.json`, `command-bridges.generated.json`, `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml:786-809`, `lanes/explicit.ts`, `scorer/projection.ts:295-300`, `lib/render.ts:200-290`, `lib/command-attach.ts:64-200`, `declared-phrase-specificity.vitest.ts`, `skill_advisor.py:4200-4215`, `derive-command-bridges.cjs`, `measure-brief-cost.mjs:20-130`, `manual-testing-playbook.md:196`, `review-brief-13.txt`, `review-scope-13.txt`, and the lineage state, registry, deltas and strategy.\n- **Core Protocol Appendix.** `spec_code` pass; `checklist_evidence` pass.\n- **Overlay Protocol Appendix.** `skill_agent` pass; `agent_cross_runtime` notApplicable; `feature_catalog_code` pass; `playbook_capability` pass.\n\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/data-13/review-report.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/data-13/review-report.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/data-13/review-report.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Report: Command Surfacing Build, Pass Thirteen - data area\\n\\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder)\\n- Pass: the thirteenth review pass, `data` area of `review/review-scope-13.txt`. It read `b8ebee37d75..932aff4e437` for `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/graph-metadata.json`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/cli-hooks-and-plugin/brief-command-policy-word.md` and `040-final-alignment-loop/decision-record.md`, then read each whole file at `932aff4e437`.\\n- Lineage: `data-13`, session `fanout-data-13-1794865302020-qunumz`, three iterations, stop reason `converged` at threshold 0.10, `blockedBy` empty. Brief `review/review-brief-13.txt`.\\n\\n## 1. Executive Summary\\n\\n- **Overall verdict: CONDITIONAL.** P0 0, P1 1, P2 2 -- the counts the verdict used.\\n- **hasAdvisories: false.** Two P2 advisories are open, but the verdict is CONDITIONAL on the active P1, so the advisory flag is not set.\\n- **Self-check outcomes.** F001 (P1) was confirmed by the full Hunter/Skeptic/Referee pass in iteration 1: every ordinary-sense prompt returned no skill under the stripped projection and the advisor at 0.82 with `passes_threshold: true` under the committed one. F002 (P2) was confirmed by the same A/B pair on the noun-phrase prompt. F003 (P2) was confirmed by running both shipped scorers on the same prompts. No finding was downgraded or called a false positive.\\n- **Review scope summary.** Three files. `graph-metadata.json` gained seven `intent_signals` phrases; the CL-009 playbook changed one prompt in three places and bumped its feature version `1.0.1.0 -> 1.0.2.0`; `decision-record.md` is new and holds ADR-001, which waives AC-004 for probe P05. The graph was recompiled: `skill-graph.json` carries the seven strings.\\n- **Operator review focus:** Review pass thirteen. First read specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-brief-13.txt and follow it: it names your area by lineage label, the scope file, the graph and stop steps each iteration runs, and the holdout rule.\\n\\n## 2. Planning Trigger\\n\\n`/speckit:plan` is required: the verdict is CONDITIONAL on one active P1.\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"triggered\\\": true,\\n  \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"CONDITIONAL\\\",\\n  \\\"hasAdvisories\\\": false,\\n  \\\"activeFindings\\\": [\\\"F001\\\", \\\"F002\\\", \\\"F003\\\"],\\n  \\\"remediationWorkstreams\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"WS-1\\\",\\n      \\\"findingIds\\\": [\\\"F001\\\"],\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P1\\\",\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Stop indexing common intent-signal words as advisor tokens\\\",\\n      \\\"scope\\\": \\\"graph-metadata intent_signals scoring surface: phrase-only author evidence, or a token stop set for the five generic signals; ordinary-sense fixtures in the specificity test\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"WS-2\\\",\\n      \\\"findingIds\\\": [\\\"F002\\\"],\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P2\\\",\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Require a phrase boundary after a declared signal\\\",\\n      \\\"scope\\\": \\\"explicit author lane phrase matching for clean arena, plus the noun-phrase fixture\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"WS-3\\\",\\n      \\\"findingIds\\\": [\\\"F003\\\"],\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P2\\\",\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Pin ordinary-sense prompts across both scorers\\\",\\n      \\\"scope\\\": \\\"declared-phrase-specificity cross-scorer cases and the Python fallback phrase reader\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"specSeed\\\": [\\n    \\\"State that an intent signal is author evidence for a phrase, and that its individual common words must not become routing tokens on their own.\\\",\\n    \\\"State that a declared signal matches a request phrase, not a longer noun phrase that happens to contain it.\\\",\\n    \\\"State that both shipped scorers must agree on the ordinary sense of every declared signal the specificity test pins.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"planSeed\\\": [\\n    \\\"Add a phrase-only path or a token stop set for the five generic signals, and add the four ordinary-sense prompts as fixtures.\\\",\\n    \\\"Require a non-word boundary after a declared signal, or record the ordinary noun-phrase sense as a negative fixture.\\\",\\n    \\\"Extend the cross-scorer case list with the ordinary-sense prompts and align the Python phrase reader if it disagrees.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"findingClasses\\\": [\\\"algorithmic\\\", \\\"algorithmic\\\", \\\"test-coverage\\\"],\\n  \\\"affectedSurfacesSeed\\\": [\\n    \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/graph-metadata.json\\\",\\n    \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/skill-graph.json\\\",\\n    \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/lanes/lexical.ts\\\",\\n    \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/lanes/explicit.ts\\\",\\n    \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/scorer/declared-phrase-specificity.vitest.ts\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"fixCompletenessRequired\\\": true\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## 3. Active Finding Registry\\n\\n| ID | Severity | Dimension | Location | Finding | Fix recommendation | Finding class | Scope proof | Affected surface hints |\\n|----|----------|-----------|----------|---------|--------------------|---------------|-------------|------------------------|\\n| F001 | P1 | correctness | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/graph-metadata.json:101` | New signals are indexed as common words, so ordinary prompts top the advisor | Score joined signals as phrases only, or exclude their single tokens from the lexical and graph lanes; add ordinary-sense fixtures | algorithmic | Four ordinary prompts return `system-skill-advisor` 0.82 `passes_threshold: true` with the committed projection and no skill with the seven signals removed | graph metadata, compiled graph, lexical lane, specificity test |\\n| F002 | P2 | correctness | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/graph-metadata.json:106` | `clean arena` fires inside a longer noun phrase and ranks the advisor above a design request | Require a phrase boundary after a declared signal, or add the noun-phrase sense as a negative fixture | algorithmic | `clean arena seating chart for the stadium` puts the advisor first at 0.82 and `sk-design` second; stripped projection returned only `sk-design` | graph metadata, explicit lane, specificity test |\\n| F003 | P2 | maintainability | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/scorer/declared-phrase-specificity.vitest.ts:169` | The declared-phrase contract holds in one scorer and not the other | Add ordinary-sense prompts as cross-scorer fixtures once the scoring fix lands | test-coverage | The native scorer returns the advisor for `the arena is clean now` and the Python fallback returns no skill; the two pinned phrases do not diverge | specificity test, `skill_advisor.py`, graph metadata |\\n\\nImpact notes:\\n\\n- F001 changes the top recommendation, not just a tail entry: `fix the routing arm in the nginx config` puts the advisor ahead of `sk-code`, and `clean arena seating chart for the stadium` puts it ahead of `sk-design`. Every case is advisory only; no command is attached and no mutating command is offered.\\n- F002 and F003 are the same signal set seen from two other angles, but each has a separate fix point: phrase boundary, and cross-scorer fixtures.\\n\\n## 4. Remediation Workstreams\\n\\n1. **WS-1 (P1)** -- Change how the five generic signals are scored. Keep `routing arm`, `clean arena`, `advisor briefs`, `arena`-family wording as phrase evidence, or drop their single tokens from the lexical and graph lanes. Accept the four ordinary-sense prompts as the regression set.\\n2. **WS-2 (P2)** -- Tighten the explicit lane's phrase boundary or record the `clean arena seating ...` sense as a negative fixture.\\n3. **WS-3 (P2)** -- Add the ordinary-sense prompts to the cross-scorer case list so the Python fallback and the native scorer cannot drift apart on this class.\\n\\n## 5. Spec Seed\\n\\n- A declared intent signal is a phrase contract, not a bag of words.\\n- A common collocation is specific only when its context is; the advisor's precision rests on that distinction.\\n- Both shipped scorers read the same declared signal list and must agree on its ordinary sense.\\n\\n## 6. Plan Seed\\n\\n- Add the phrase-only/token-stop behavior to the signal scoring path and extend `declared-phrase-specificity.vitest.ts` with the four prompts.\\n- Add the noun-phrase negative fixture and the boundary rule.\\n- Add the cross-scorer fixture and align the Python phrase reader where it disagrees.\\n\\n## 7. Traceability Status\\n\\nCore protocols:\\n\\n- `spec_code`: pass. The seven signals match T006's description (`040/tasks.md:49`) and the compiled `skill-graph.json` carries them; ADR-001 (`decision-record.md:37`), AC-004 (`acceptance-criteria.md:59`) and `probes.json` agree on P05 and P07-P09.\\n- `checklist_evidence`: pass. `probes.json` P05 is `command-doctor-helper` at 0.8 and P07/P08/P09 top the advisor; the final-tree rerun reproduces P05 at 0.8.\\n\\nOverlay protocols:\\n\\n- `skill_agent`: pass. The authored metadata and the compiled graph carry identical strings; no agent file is in this area.\\n- `agent_cross_runtime`: notApplicable. No runtime mirror or agent definition is touched.\\n- `feature_catalog_code`: pass. `scorer-fusion/five-lane-fusion.md:27` documents the lexical lane as token overlap, so the observed token behavior matches the documented design; the defect is the signal list's word choice, not the lane.\\n- `playbook_capability`: pass. `check for skilled updates` tops `command-doctor-update` at 0.8962 and renders `system-skilled-doctor → /doctor:update (ask)` in a parent and `(parent-named only)` in a child, matching `brief-command-policy-word.md:148` and `:160-161`.\\n\\n`AC_COVERAGE`: **exempt**. The target spec folder has no `acceptance-criteria.md` and no `implementation-summary.md` at its own level; the phase children own their AC coverage.\\n\\n## 8. Deferred Items\\n\\n- The phrase `update skilled to the latest version` is still a declared `/doctor:update` trigger (`_routes.yaml:804`) but scores `sk-git` and never returns its command. The playbook avoids it now. The route file is outside this area, so this is deferred to a routing-area pass, not reported against the playbook.\\n- The Python fallback has no command-bridge layer, so P05 there returns `system-skill-advisor` rather than `command-doctor-helper`. That is a scorer-scope difference, not an ADR-001 contradiction.\\n- The `derived` block was not regenerated with the seven signals; a fresh extractor run does not add them to `trigger_phrases` or `keywords`, so this is not a stale routing surface.\\n- Holdout hygiene is clean for this area: the bridge generator reads route YAML and scorer sources, and `measure-brief-cost.mjs:124` refuses holdout rows.\\n\\n## Dimension Expansion Map\\n\\n- Completed pivots: 0. Failed pivots: 0. Audited overrides: 0.\\n- Saturated directions: none. Pivot lineage: none.\\n- Selected review directions: correctness and traceability (iteration 1), security and maintainability (iteration 2), all four as final verification (iteration 3).\\n- Remaining frontier: none. This section records breadth only and does not change the verdict.\\n\\n## 9. Search Ledger\\n\\n`*No search-depth state captured (legacy v1 record)*`\\n\\nThe probes that stand in for a search ledger in this pass:\\n\\n- Native scorer A/B: committed projection vs the seven signals removed, over eight ordinary prompts; four flip to the advisor, two change rank, two are unchanged.\\n- Signal list: 39 entries, 0 duplicates, no control, shell or JSON metacharacter.\\n- Playbook: `check for skilled updates` -> `command-doctor-update` 0.8962; old prompt -> `sk-git`; rendered labels match parent and child expectations.\\n- ADR: P05 tops `command-doctor-helper` at 0.8 before and after the signals.\\n- Cross-scorer: native vs Python over the same prompts; two divergences, both on the new phrases.\\n- Holdout: generator input list and the refusal path read; no corpus row reaches a generation or report path.\\n- State: three iteration records, three deltas whose first line equals its record, one registry with three open findings, four dimensions covered.\\n\\n## 10. Audit Appendix\\n\\n- **Convergence.** Iteration 3 returned `STOP`, `converged`, score 1.0, `blockedBy` `[]`. Ratios were 1.0, 0.1429, 0.0.\\n- **Coverage.** 4 of 4 dimensions; core protocols `spec_code` and `checklist_evidence` each recorded; overlay protocols recorded as pass or notApplicable.\\n- **Ruled-out claims.** A stale derived block; a holdout leak through bridge generation; secret or environment exposure in the playbook; JSON or shell injection through a signal; duplicate-signal amplification; the waived P05 returning to the advisor; a mid-pass change between iteration 1 and the final tree.\\n- **Sources reviewed.** `graph-metadata.json` (whole file and the signal block), `brief-command-policy-word.md` (whole file and the changed ranges), `decision-record.md`, `040/acceptance-criteria.md:59`, `040/tasks.md:37-121`, `040/scratch/probes.json`, `skill-graph.json`, `command-bridges.generated.json`, `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml:786-809`, `lanes/explicit.ts`, `scorer/projection.ts:295-300`, `lib/render.ts:200-290`, `lib/command-attach.ts:64-200`, `declared-phrase-specificity.vitest.ts`, `skill_advisor.py:4200-4215`, `derive-command-bridges.cjs`, `measure-brief-cost.mjs:20-130`, `manual-testing-playbook.md:196`, `review-brief-13.txt`, `review-scope-13.txt`, and the lineage state, registry, deltas and strategy.\\n- **Core Protocol Appendix.** `spec_code` pass; `checklist_evidence` pass.\\n- **Overlay Protocol Appendix.** `skill_agent` pass; `agent_cross_runtime` notApplicable; `feature_catalog_code` pass; `playbook_capability` pass.\\n\\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/data-13/review-report.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794866512114,"end":1794866542102}}}}
